9:- **Keeping the expected type at a call written `f(x)` is four one-token edits, and it clears the natives only by binding `Bottom`** (`reviews/numerics-plan-coordinator/measure-D.md`, a classpath shadow of `Operators.scala`, programs and captures under `reviews/numerics-plan-coordinator/probes-D/`; row 455). The parser builds `f(x)` as a tight juxtaposition with `fnApp = false` (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/parser/Expression.rats:548-556`), which the checker takes through `ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/scala_src/typechecker/impls/Operators.scala:76-86`, `:336-345` and `:197`; `:89-90`, the `fnApp = true` form, is reached only by desugarings, and editing it alone changes nothing. The four edits are on the tree with the retry (`Operators.scala:85`, `:90`, `:197`, `:345`; "The compiled checker infers a generic's static arguments with coercion ..." below): an attempt is kept only when its result converts to the expected type, and a call written `f(x)` that no attempt keeps is typed as without the context, the binding then reporting a call the rule accepts. With the context passed, a result-only `T` becomes `BottomType`, not the expected type, wherever the context is a plain type (a typed binding, a function's or method's body, an `if` branch, a statement, `builtinPrimitive(…)`, `fail(…)`), because the context adds only an upper bound and the solver binds the join of the lower bounds, of which there is none; the expected type itself is inferred only where `T` sits invariantly inside it (`a: BoxT[\ZZ64\] = mkB()` checks with `T = ZZ64`). A method invocation binds `BottomType` the same way (`x: ZZ64 = Fac.make()`), and under the compile path's `Object` bound every one of these shapes is `BottomType`, context or not. Of the natives' result-only errors the context clears all but those where the expected type is dropped elsewhere (an `if` with no `else`, a `typecase` `else`, a `let` body, a loose juxtaposition `fail "…"`) and three that carry the phrase in their message: the tuple comparisons (`Library/FortressLibrary.fss:169`), a `fail` inside a `for` body (`Library/RangeInternals.fss:157`) and `List`'s nullary comprehension (`Library/List.fss:150`). On the library, measurement D's `DArg` gives 1 error, `a03` (`s: String = idt(3)`) refused by the binding; `DCtx` 3; and `DComp`'s `k01` checks with `T = ZZ64` (`compile-ladder/rung-inference-checker/probes/onelib/`, `probes/dcomp/`). The method, prefix, infix and parenthesised forms under a context take their numerals (`probes/repair/SkCtxForms.diff.txt`); an enclosing call's argument and a loose juxtaposition drop the context (`ProjectFortress/compiler_tests/XXXInferContextDrops.fss`). Not probed: what code generation makes of the natives' `BottomType`. The binding of a result-only `T` to `Bottom` is the checker's today: an inference variable left open is bound to `BOTTOM` (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/scala_src/useful/STypesUtil.scala:1954-1955`, `killIvars`). The paper's i
